 In the R137 example, model_level values entries are {\"model\": \"G1.6\", \"value\": 2.5} with unit_symbol at attribute level: {\"attribute\": \"qmax\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [...]}. Yes — unit at the attribute level for model_level. Similarly config_level: axis values {condition, value, unit_symbol}. Good, follow the examples.\n\nFor model_level string attributes (software_checksum, connection_thread, pressure_loss_class), value is string, unit_symbol null (omit or include). I'll include unit_symbol only where meaningful; omit elsewhere.\n\nRanges in model_level values: ratio_q3_q1 range objects. value: {min: 125, max: 500}. OK.\n\nbattery_quantity: value {min:2,max:3} or 1.\n\nNow write the models[] entries. Include label. attributes: I'll mirror key values.\n\nM1 attributes:\n{\n \"nominal_diameter\": {\"value\": 15, \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\"},\n \"permanent_flowrate_q3\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\"},\n \"overload_flowrate_q4\": {\"value\": 2, \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\"},\n \"ratio_q3_q1\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 125, \"max\": 500}, \"unit_symbol\": \"R\"},\n \"software_version\": {\"value\": \"V1.3\"},\n \"software_checksum\": {\"value\": \"25667\"},\n \"pressure_loss\": {\"value\": 0.4, \"unit_symbol\": \"bar\"},\n \"pressure_loss_class\": {\"value\": \"Δp40\"},\n \"battery\": {\"value\": \"2 or 3 non-replaceable lithium batteries, Umin 2.7 V, Umax 3.7 V, life time up to 16 years\"}\n}\n\nThat duplicates model_level but attributes on models help consumers. Include. It's verbose but complete. Actually to control output size, maybe trim attributes to fewer keys: nominal_diameter, permanent_flowrate_q3, software_checksum. The model_level has everything. I'll keep attributes moderate: dn, q3, checksum, q4. Plus label text covering the rest? Let me include: nominal_diameter, permanent_flowrate_q3, overload_flowrate_q4, software_checksum. Good.\n\nLabels: \"DN15, Q3 = 1.6 m³/h, software 13, checksum 25667 (Δp40, battery 2–3 pcs)\" — maybe simpler: label \"UWM DN15 Q3=1.6 checksum 25667\". Keep label same as model_id? Model_id can be \"DN15_Q3=1.6_ck25667\" and label \"UWM DN15, Q3 = 1.6 m³/h, software 13, checksum 25667\". Then values[] refs use model_id (short). Shorter ids reduce output size. Let me use:\n\nmodel_id: \"DN15_Q3=1.6_ck25667\"? Hmm \"ck\" nonstandard. Use \"DN15 Q3=1.6 (25667)\". Model IDs:\n- \"DN15 Q3=1.6 (25667)\"\n- \"DN15 Q3=2.5 (25667)\"\n- \"DN20 Q3=2.5 (25667)\"\n- \"DN20 Q3=4 (25667)\"\n- \"DN15 Q3=1.6 (21574)\"\n- \"DN15 Q3=2.5 (21574)\"\n- \"DN20 Q3=2.5 (22681)\"\n- \"DN20 Q3=4 (22681)\"\n\nLabels: \"UWM DN15, Q3 = 1.6 m³/h, software 13, checksum 25667\". Good.\n\nfamily_name: \"UWM\".\n\nNow matrix_tables names must tie to models: I'll reference in description: \"Corresponds to model DN15 Q3=1.6 (25667).\"\n\nLet me now also double check q2 values in 3.2: \"25, 20, 16, 12,7, 10, 8, 6,35, 5\" → 25, 20, 16, 12.7, 10, 8, 6.35, 5. Yes.\n\n3.3 Q1: 20, 15.625, 12.5, 10, 7.94, 6.25, 5; Q2: 32, 25, 20, 16, 12.7, 10, 8. R: 125,160,200,250,315,400,500.\n\n3.4 Q1: 25, 20, 16, 12.7, 10, 8, 6.35, 5; Q2: 40, 32, 25.6, 20.32, 16, 12.8, 10.16, 8; R: 160,200,250,315,400,500,630,800.\n\n3.5 Q1: 12.8, 10, 8, 6.4; Q2: 20.48, 16, 12.8, 10.24; R: 125,160,200,250.\n\n3.6 Q1: 15.625, 12.5, 10, 7.94, 6.25; Q2: 25, 20, 16, 12.7, 10; R: 160,200,250,315,400.\n\n3.7 Q1: 20, 15.625, 12.5, 10; Q2: 32, 25, 20, 16; R: 125,160,200,250.\n\n3.8 Q1: 20, 16, 12.7, 10; Q2: 32, 25.6, 20.32, 16; R: 200,250,315,400.\n\nGood.\n\nNow compose final JSON. Ensure valid JSON: escape nothing weird; Unicode fine (m³, Δ, ¾, °, ₀ subscripts — I'll use \"Q3\" plain to be safe with snake_case; descriptions can contain Q₃ but I'll use plain Q3).\n\ncertificate:\n{\n \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-SK1-20.02 Rev. 1\",\n \"scheme\": \"A\",\n \"page_total\": 10,\n \"member_state\": \"Slovakia\",\n \"date_issued\": \"2025-11-06\",\n \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"SK1\"\n}\n\nissuing_authority:\n{\n \"name\": \"Slovak Legal Metrology (SLM)\",\n \"address_lines\": [\"Geologická 9966/1\", \"821 06 Bratislava-Podunajské Biskupice, Slovakia\", \"Product Certification Body\", \"Hviedzoslavova 31\", \"974 01 Banská Bystrica, Slovakia\"],\n \"person_responsible\": \"Dušan Šmigura\",\n \"person_title\": \"Director of PCB\",\n \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"SK1\"\n}\n\napplicants: [{name, address_lines [\"68, West Town Road, Shangtian Town, Fenghua\", \"Zhejiang, China 3155\"]}]\n\nmanufacturers: same.\n\ncertified_type:\n{\n \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n \"type_designations\": [\"UWM\"],\n \"module_designation\": \"Ultrasonic water meter intended for the metering of cold potable water\",\n \"description\": \"Compact ultrasonic water meter with electronic indication device for measuring, memorising and displaying the volume of cold potable water passing through the measurement transducer at metering conditions. Measurement based on the ultrasonic bidirectional transit-time principle. Intended for clean water in residential, commercial and light industrial use; can be installed in all positions; not designed to measure reverse flow.\"\n}\n\nmodel_family: family_name \"UWM\", models 8.\n\ncomponents: flow_sensor, calculator_and_indication_device, battery (OR options), non_return_valve, communication_interface.\n\ncharacteristics: type_level {...}, model_level [...], config_level [...].\n\nmatrix_tables: 10.\n\nrecommendation: {id: \"R49\", edition: 2013, amendment: null, scheme: \"A\", accuracy_classes: [\"2\"]}.\n\nHmm amendment: omit (null allowed? schema shows amendment field; omit if not present — rule 8 says omit absent fields; but null is in shape... I'll omit).\n\ntest_reports, revision_history as above.\n\nfootnotes: omit (none).\n\nOne more consideration: \"Ratio to R800\" added in Rev 1 — meaning R800 ratio option added. Fine, captured in tables.\n\nBattery component alternatives: alternatives: \"OR\", characteristics: {\"option_1\": \"two or three non-replaceable lithium batteries, Umax = 3.7 V, life time up to 