odel_level values — just numeric or range; per example {\"model\": \"G1.6\", \"value\": 2.5}. No unit per entry. Footnote markers none.\n\nconfig_level example shape from schema: values[]: {condition, value}. Rule 5: \"Values follow the same structured form: {condition, value, unit_symbol}\". So config values include unit_symbol per entry. I'll do that.\n\nconfig_level entry 1: temperature_class:\n{\n \"attribute\": \"temperature_class\",\n \"axis\": \"body_material\",\n \"values\": [\n   {\"condition\": \"brass body\", \"value\": \"T30, T50, T70\"},\n   {\"condition\": \"plastic body\", \"value\": \"T30, T50\"}\n ]\n}\n\nentry 2: water_temperature_range:\n{\n \"attribute\": \"water_temperature_range\",\n \"axis\": \"temperature_class_and_body_material\",\n \"values\": [\n  {\"condition\": \"T30 (brass and plastic body)\", \"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 30}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"T50 (brass and plastic body)\", \"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 50}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"},\n  {\"condition\": \"T70 (brass body)\", \"value\": {\"min\": 0.1, \"max\": 70}, \"unit_symbol\": \"°C\"}\n ]\n}\n\nentry 3: electromagnetic_class axis body_material: brass → \"E1\", plastic → \"E1, E2\".\n\nentry 4: maximum_permissible_error_upper_range axis water_temperature:\n{\"condition\": \"water temperature ≤ 30 °C\", \"value\": {\"min\": -2, \"max\": 2}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"},\n{\"condition\": \"water temperature > 30 °C\", \"value\": {\"min\": -3, \"max\": 3}, \"unit_symbol\": \"%\"}\n\nGood.\n\nNow finalize model_level entries with 8 values each.\n\nLet me write values arrays.\n\nnominal_diameter (mm):\n[{\"model\":\"DN15 Q3=1.6 (25667)\",\"value\":15},{\"model\":\"DN15 Q3=2.5 (25667)\",\"value\":15},{\"model\":\"DN20 Q3=2.5 (25667)\",\"value\":20},{\"model\":\"DN20 Q3=4 (25667)\",\"value\":20},{\"model\":\"DN15 Q3=1.6 (21574)\",\"value\":15},{\"model\":\"DN15 Q3=2.5 (21574)\",\"value\":15},{\"model\":\"DN20 Q3=2.5 (22681)\",\"value\":20},{\"model\":\"DN